+**Physical carrier bridge (carrierFormat).** The project grant-journal carrier has its
+own format axis, and it is not the state schema. Detection on open is by schema
+introspection only, because the oldest format carries no version row. Reader staging
+mirrors the root-reader and state-decoder pattern: a core supporting only carrierFormat
+{1, 2} refuses a carrierFormat 3 carrier **typed** and keeps its prior generation until it
+expires; a carrierFormat {1, 2, 3} core reads both, under recordSchema-1 semantics for
+historical generations and recordSchema-3 for current ones. A historical `platform` value
+is surfaced as a historical alias and is never presented as an S8 machine id, rewritten,
+or joined to `RepoExecutionGrantV2.platformId`.
+
+**Carrier migration is NOT an installation transition.** It does not use the S9.2 intent
+or journal, and it cannot: reusing the closed logical `store-migrate` intent with an
+unchanged state schema and store generation refuses
+`TRANSITION.MIGRATE_REQUIRES_SCHEMA_ADVANCE` and
+`TRANSITION.SCHEMA_CHANGE_SELECTS_NEW_STORE`, and an invented `carrier-migrate` operation
+refuses `TRANSITION.OPERATION`. `InstallationTransitionIntentV1` is a closed 11-member
+record and `InstallationTransitionJournalV1` a closed 20-member record; neither has a
+carrier field. Migration 1 or 2 → 3 is instead a **selected prospective expansion** of
+the existing `store-gc` operation (security-owned, `authorizationClass:
+exclusive-lease`, `writesTrackedIntent: false`): the inherited row shows only that
+`store-gc` is not an intent-writing transition, not that this mutation was already
+authorized, so the added per-namespace behaviour is selected here explicitly. It runs
+under the install fence with non-blocking `EXCLUSIVE` on
+the affected project namespace, where a busy namespace is skipped and retained exactly as
+GC already behaves. Its state is reported through the existing `store-status`
+`migration-state` field. It is additive, disables no inherited constraint or trigger, and
+rewrites no inherited row. Three atomic durable acts in order — `TERMINAL` append, object
+creation, format-row publication — with the format ROW as the commit point and detection
+keyed on that row, so every durable prefix has an exact resume action. Protocol:
+`design-corrections/security/carrier-migration.v1.md`. A format-unaware core cannot be
+made to refuse a migrated carrier, so a generation at or above `first_generation`
+appearing in the inherited table is a detectable split-brain custody condition, never
+valid history; the mitigation is the existing ordered-release pattern.
+
+**Grant-generation closure gains a third cause.** The inherited rule (security v8 §5.4
